title: BadEnd
---
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
<<show ScreenBlocker>>
<<play_music MainTheme>>
The silence after the screen dies is total. Absolute. The kind that fills every corner and presses against the inside of your skull.
I sit in the chair for a long time. I don't move. I don't think. I just exist in the quiet, the way I've always existed in it.
<<if $negSelfPerception > $posSelfPerception>>
    Nothing changed. That's the thing that gets me.
    I met an alien. A real, living being from another world. They reached across the entire void of space to talk to me. And I still couldn't make it work.
    I think about every wrong thing I said. Every wall I put up. Every moment I chose distance over connection.
    The pattern is clear. It was never about space or aliens or missions. It's me. I do this to everything.
<<else>>
    I tell myself it was never going to work. Different species, different worlds, too much history between our families. The odds were against us from the start.
    It almost sounds convincing.
<<endif>>
The mission continues. I write reports. I enter cryosleep. I wake up.
Days pass. Then months. Then years.
{$catName}'s frequency never lights up again. The comms buffer stays empty. The translator has nothing to render.
I never find out what happened to them. Whether their people locked them down, whether they found someone else to talk to, whether they're okay.
I never find out, because I never became the kind of person who deserved to know.
The ship carries me closer to the star. Eventually I'm close enough to study the dark spot, the whole reason I was sent out here.
It's gone.
The star is whole. Smooth. Unbroken. As if nothing was ever wrong with it.
I check the instruments. I recalibrate. I check again. Nothing. The anomaly that consumed six expeditions and my father simply doesn't exist anymore.
I don't even feel surprised. Just tired. The universe gave me two mysteries, and I solved neither of them.
I file a report nobody will read and enter cryosleep for the long trip back to a planet that won't notice I returned.
The ship hums. The stars don't answer. And the silence, which once felt like it might break open into something new, closes back around me like it never left.
<<detour End>>
<<the_end "ENDING: Static">>
===
